CARSHARING 2017 DEMAND & WEATHER REPORT
SQL Analysis Report for the Marketing Team
Database: carsharing | Analysis period: 2017
Executive Summary

The 2017 CarSharing analysis identified clear patterns in demand across time, weekday, month, season and temperature. The highest single demand rate was 6.46 on 15 June 2017 at 17:00. Saturday had the highest average weekday demand at 4.61, July had the highest monthly average at 4.91, and Fall had the highest seasonal average at 4.77.
Mild conditions were the most prevalent temperature category at 48.64%, while Clear or partly cloudy was the most prevalent weather condition at 67.28%. Despite Mild weather being most common, Hot conditions produced the highest average demand at 4.97. These findings provide useful guidance for demand-focused marketing and operational planning.
