6. Marketing Interpretation and Recommendations
Target the 17:00 period: Both Saturday and Thursday recorded their highest hourly average demand at 17:00. Marketing offers, vehicle availability and customer engagement should be strong around this period.
Prioritize warmer conditions: Hot weather had the highest average demand at 4.97, despite Mild being the most prevalent category. Weather-based promotions can therefore be especially valuable during warmer periods.
Focus on July and Fall: July recorded the highest monthly average demand at 4.91, while Fall was the strongest season at 4.77.
Use clear-weather opportunities: Clear or partly cloudy weather represented 67.28% of observations. This is the dominant environment in which the service operates and should be considered in campaign planning.
Reduce emphasis during overnight lows: Demand was particularly weak around 03:00-05:00 on the selected weekdays. Promotional and operational resources could be reduced during these periods.
Monitor weather variability: July illustrates that demand differs across weather conditions, so campaigns can be adjusted according to weather forecasts rather than relying solely on calendar periods.
Conclusion
The 2017 analysis indicates that demand was strongest during warmer conditions, in July, during Fall, and around the 17:00 period. Saturday was the strongest weekday by average demand. The weather environment was predominantly Mild and Clear or partly cloudy, while Hot conditions generated the highest average demand. These findings can help the marketing team schedule campaigns around high-demand periods, tailor promotions to warmer weather, and manage resources more efficiently during low-demand overnight periods.

